Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement. Question: Is "financial point of view" the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior? Option A: No Option B: Yes

Merger Agreement Excerpt: Section 8.1 – Dual Consideration Protocol. Notwithstanding any other provision in this Agreement, prior to effecting any Change of Recommendation or initiating negotiations to invalidate a Superior Proposal, the Company's Board shall assemble a special advisory panel consisting of independent financial, strategic, and legal experts. The Board’s determination that an Acquisition Proposal is superior shall be based on an integrated evaluation that includes: (i) detailed financial metrics including pricing, financing structures, and profitability forecasts; (ii) an assessment of the proposal’s alignment with the Company's long-term strategic objectives; (iii) operational synergy potential; and (iv) any regulatory and legal implications as advised by external counsel. Furthermore, any amendments to a proposal that affect these metrics shall trigger a re-evaluation period of three Business Days. Importantly, the Agreement expressly mandates that reliance solely on the financial point of view is prohibited in these determinations. (Pages 120-122)
